"text/css\" href=\"/static/base/1.0.1/css/abs.css\">\n117\t<div id=\"content-inner\">\n118\t  <div id=\"abs\">\n119\t    <div class=\"dateline\">\n120\t  [Submitted on 31 Jul 2026]</div>\n121\t    <h1 class=\"title mathjax\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Title:</span>Do Music Foundation Models Embed Pitch in Helical Structure?</h1>\n122\t    <div class=\"authors\"><span class=\"descriptor\">Authors:</span><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Yagi,+H\" rel=\"nofollow\">Hayato Yagi</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Takamichi,+S\" rel=\"nofollow\">Shinnosuke Takamichi</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Sato,+R\" rel=\"nofollow\">Rin Sato</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Tanaka,+K\" rel=\"nofollow\">Keitaro Tanaka</a>, <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/search/cs?searchtype=author&amp;query=Morishima,+S\" rel=\"nofollow\">Shigeo Morishima</a></div>            <div id=\"download-button-info\" hidden>View a PDF of the paper titled Do Music Foundation Models Embed Pitch in Helical Structure?, by Hayato Yagi and 4 other authors</div>\n123\t    <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"/pdf/2607.29086v1\">View PDF</a>\n124\t    <a class=\"mobile-submission-download\" href=\"https://arxiv.org/html/2607.29086v1\">HTML (experimental)</a>\n125\t\n126\t\n127\t\n128\t    <blockquote class=\"abstract mathjax\">\n129\t            <span class=\"descriptor\">Abstract:</span>This study analyzes the intermediate representations of music foundation models (MFMs) and reports the geometric structures used to represent pitch information. By inputting isolated musical notes into trained MFMs and analyzing their principal components, we reveal that the representations form a helical structure reflecting the octave periodicity of pitch. Furthermore, we show that the clarity and geometry of this helical structure vary not only across models but also with the acoustic properties of the input signals. Our analysis provides a novel approach for clarifying the internal mechanisms of MFMs.\n130\t    </blockquote>\n131\t\n132\t    <!--CONTEXT-->\n133\t    <div class=\"metatable\">\n134\t      <table summary=\"Additional metadata\">        <tr>\n135\t          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Comments:</td>\n136\t          <td class=\"tablecell comments mathjax\">Accepted by ISMIR 2026</td>\n137\t        </tr>\n138\t<tr>\n139\t          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Subjects:</td>\n140\t          <td class=\"tablecell subjects\">\n141\t            <span class=\"primary-subject\">Sound (cs.SD)</span></td>\n142\t        </tr><tr>\n143\t          <td class=\"tablecell label\">Cite as:</td>\n144\t          <td class=\"tablecell arxivid\"><span class=\"arxivid\"><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.29086\">arXiv:2607.29086</a> [cs.SD]</span></td>\n145\t        </tr>\n146\t        <tr>\n147\t          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n148\t          <td class=\"tablecell arxividv\">(or <span class=\"arxivid\">\n149\t              <a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.29086v1\">arXiv:2607.29086v1</a> [cs.SD]</span> for this version)\n150\t          </td>\n151\t        </tr>\n152\t        <tr>\n153\t          <td class=\"tablecell label\">&nbsp;</td>\n154\t          <td class=\"tablecell arxivdoi\">              <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2607.29086\" id=\"arxiv-doi-link\">https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2607.29086</a><div class=\"button-and-tooltip\">\n155\t              <button class=\"more-info\" aria-describedby=\"more-info-desc-1\">\n156\t                <svg height=\"15\" role=\"presentation\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 512 512\"><path fill=\"currentColor\" d=\"M256 8C119.043 8 8 119.083 8 256c0 136.997 111.043 248 248 248s248-111.003 248-248C504 119.083 392.957 8 256 8zm0 110c23.196 0 42 18.804 42 42s-18.804 42-42 42-42-18.804-42-42 18.804-42 42-42zm56 254c0 6.627-5.373 12-12 12h-88c-6.627